			"date": "2026-06-03T00:06:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Hmm...</p><p>State of CSS 2025 has it's gender question on the last page with 69% completion rate.</p><p>You would assume that a bunch of users skipped that question.</p><p>Looking back at the first page of the survey: 99% of users answered the first question of the first page, but only 74% of users answered the last question of the first page.</p><p>At 5 pages, there's a quick falloff of users answering questions, but the gender question was answered by almost everyone who made it to the end.</p>",
